        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Don't Leave Money on the Table!</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/49267.webp" alt="Don't Leave Money on the Table!" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>This Friday, September 19<sup>th</sup> at 5 pm marks the deadline for the Community Foundation of Teton Valley’s 3<sup>rd</sup> Quarter Grant Cycle.  If you are a local 501(c)3 public charity, local school or local government entity you are eligible to apply for grant funds made possible through the Tin Cup Challenger Fund. Don’t leave money on the table that could help you in addressing the critical needs that your organization serves in our community!</p>
<p>“We are very grateful to our Community Challengers who make our grants program possible each year through their gifts to the Tin Cup Challenger Fund.  Teton Valley would be a much different place without our nonprofit organizations. We are proud to support their compelling work and help further their impact within our community,” says Carrie Mowrey, Executive Director of the Community Foundation of Teton Valley.</p>
<p>The Community Foundation of Teton Valley Grants Program funds requests up to $2,500 per year for local nonprofit organizations, on an ongoing basis, as funds allow.   The Grants Committee may consider grants larger than $2,500 for exceptional projects, or for collaborations involving more than one local nonprofit organization.  The Community Foundation Grants Program supports a wide variety of proposals, including those seeking to address issues in the arts, environment, social services, education, recreation, animal care and civic arenas. Additionally, the Community Foundation of Teton Valley financially supports local nonprofits with strategic planning, programs, capital projects, equipment purchases, pilot projects, and more. Applications must demonstrate a community need and granted funds must directly benefit residents of Teton Valley.  For more information, or to download a grant application, <a title="Grants" href="https://cftetonvalley.org/nonprofits/grants/">CLICK HERE</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Don’t leave money on the table, submit your grant application by 5pm on Friday, September 19<sup>th</sup> and let us help you better serve the Teton Valley community!</strong></p>
